_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Match token candidates by earliest position, not candidate order.**

Line 238 currently picks the first candidate that matches, which can select a later occurrence when URL tokens allow both `'.../'` and `'...'`. This can make the wrong URL substring tappable.



<details>
<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 _TokenMatch? _findTokenMatch(String content, SerializableToken token, int cursor) {
   final candidates = _displayCandidates(token);
   if (candidates.isEmpty) return _TokenMatch(start: cursor, end: cursor);

+  _TokenMatch? bestMatch;
   for (final candidate in candidates) {
     final start = content.indexOf(candidate, cursor);
     if (start >= 0) {
-      return _TokenMatch(start: start, end: start + candidate.length);
+      final match = _TokenMatch(start: start, end: start + candidate.length);
+      if (bestMatch == null ||
+          match.start < bestMatch.start ||
+          (match.start == bestMatch.start && match.end > bestMatch.end)) {
+        bestMatch = match;
+      }
     }
   }

-  return null;
+  return bestMatch;
 }
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@lib/widgets/message_content_text.dart` around lines 238 - 243, The loop over
candidates currently returns the first candidate that matches (based on
candidate order) which can pick a later occurrence; instead scan all candidates
to find the earliest match position (minimum start) and return a single
_TokenMatch with that start and corresponding end; update the code using the
existing variables candidates, content, cursor, start, end and construct/return
the _TokenMatch for the minimum start found (or null/no match if none).
```

</details>

